{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtvRA17NrkKwHwvufAPa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A clue is visible. How often the thinking itself contains a \\boxed falls steadily as induction is weakened: 69% (brake only) → 54% (E1) → 46% (gate) → 28% (seven heads zeroed). Only 3 of the 14 no-box answers had a \\boxed in their thinking. So the answer line seems to draw the \\boxed format either from an earlier \\boxed in the thinking (an induction-like copy) or from the instruction. The prompt tokens are \" \\\\\" (1088) + \"boxed\" (76367), while the line-start token emitted is \"\\\\\" (59). Retrieval from the instruction is therefore not a pure same-token copy. Before spending a forward pass on attention patterns, I'll do a weight-only screen. For every full-attention head, I'll compute the OV-circuit logit effect from source tokens \"boxed\"/\" \\\\\" onto the target \"\\\\\" and \"boxed\", z-scored over the vocabulary. If one of the four tier-2 gated heads stands out, it is the prime candidate for exemption; if none does, the format route is more distributed and I need the attention data.\n\n```python\n# Weight-only screen: which FA heads' OV circuits map source 'boxed'(76367)/' \\\\'(1088) onto target '\\\\'(59)/'boxed'? z-scored over vocab.\nE = load('model.language_model.embed_tokens.weight')  # tied unembedding (read-only use)\nEn = E / E.norm(dim=1, keepdim=True).mean()\ndef head_ov_effect(L, h, src_ids):\n    Wq = None\n    Wv = load(f'model.language_model.layers.{L}.self_attn.v_proj.weight'); Wo = load(f'model.language_model.layers.{L}.self_attn.o_proj.weight')\n    lnw = load(f'model.language_model.layers.{L}.input_layernorm.weight')\n    kv = h // 4; Vh = Wv[kv*256:(kv+1)*256]; Oh = Wo[:, h*256:(h+1)*256]\n    x = E[src_ids]; x = x / x.pow(2).mean(-1,keepdim=True).sqrt() * (1+lnw)\n    out = (x @ Vh.T) @ Oh.T                       # [n_src, 1024]\n    logits = out @ E.T                            # [n_src, vocab]\n    z = (logits - logits.mean(1,keepdim=True)) / logits.std(1,keepdim=True)\n    return z\nres_ov=[]\nfor L in [3,7,11,15,19,23]:\n    for h in range(8):\n        z = head_ov_effect(L,h,[76367,1088])\n        res_ov.append((L,h, float(z[0,59]), float(z[0,76367]), float(z[1,59]), float(z[1,76367])))\ngated={(11,1),(15,7),(19,5),(23,0),(23,4),(23,5),(23,7)}\nres_ov.sort(key=lambda r:-max(r[2],r[4]))\nfor r in res_ov[:12]: print(('G ' if (r[0],r[1]) in gated else '  ')+f\"L{r[0]}H{r[1]}: boxed->\\\\ {r[2]:+.1f} boxed->boxed {r[3]:+.1f} | \\\\->\\\\ {r[4]:+.1f} \\\\->boxed {r[5]:+.1f}\")\nprint('gated heads:', [(f\"L{r[0]}H{r[1]}\", round(r[2],1), round(r[4],1)) for r in res_ov if (r[0],r[1]) in gated])\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5101,"cache_read_input_tokens":56459,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5101},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e01c29c3-4f30-44c6-bee0-870b4ff8f3f8","uuid":"31f7e86d-b855-4500-b8fa-2eb702d8da90","timestamp":"2026-11-10T08:21:08.216Z","request_id":"req_011CgtvR95YfFE7Bg72CmF7k"}
